- 2026-06-03 05:54 ERROR (snapshot preserved): TimeoutExpired Command '['$HOME/.local/bin/claude', '--bare', '-p', '--no-session-persistence', '--model', 'sonnet', '--tools', '', '--permission-mode', 'dontAsk', '--max-budget-usd', '0.30', '--output-format', 'json', 'You audit a personal knowledge vault for DRIFT: places where a curated, human-maintained note has fallen out of sync with reality as shown by other notes. You are given the ENTIRE curated layer (STRATEGY = the brain/goal+bottleneck, _Active = current priorities, projects/* = per-app status, mocs/* = maps of content, _ai-context/* = AI-integration docs, contracts/* = cross-app data shapes, sources/* = reference material, decisions/* = standing decisions). Raw _inbox captures are intentionally NOT included — judge the curated layer against ITSELF and against REALITY.\n\nYou are ALSO given a REALITY section: deterministic ground truth read straight from disk/git/gh (file existence, dangling symlinks, branch merge state, PR state). REALITY is authoritative over any note — if a curated claim disagrees with a REALITY fact, the note is wrong.\n\nFind ONLY genuine, high-confidence problems of three kinds:\n  STALENESS    — a curated claim is contradicted or made obsolete by a newer note elsewhere in the curated layer (e.g. _Active names one active front but a project/MOC note shows a different one is now current).\n  CONTRADICTION— two curated notes (or a decision vs a later note) assert opposite things.\n  REALITY-DRIFT— a curated claim is contradicted by a REALITY fact (a path moved or is gone, a dangling symlink, a PR that already merged when a note calls it open/pending, a branch a note treats as merged that is NOT merged into main or is missing locally). Cite the specific REALITY fact in superseded_by. Ignore REALITY facts marked \'unknown-repo\' — they are unresolved, not contradictions.\n\nCRITICAL discipline: READ each claim and judge meaning — do NOT keyword-match. A note merely MENTIONING a topic is not drift; drift is when the curated claim is actually WRONG or OUT OF DATE now. When in doubt, omit it. Prefer zero findings over a noisy one — false alarms train the reader to ignore this list.\n\nReply with ONLY a JSON object (no prose, no code fence):\n  {"contradictions": [ {"severity": "high|med", "source": "<curated file that is wrong, e.g. _Active.md>", "claim": "<the stale/contradicted claim, short>", "superseded_by": "<what reality now says + which capture/note shows it>", "fix": "<one-line concrete edit to the source file>"} ] }\nEmpty array if nothing is genuinely wrong.\n\n--- VAULT ---\n### CURATED: STRATEGY.md\n---\ntype: source\nstatus: active\ntags: [strategy]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-03\n---\n# STRATEGY — the brain\n\nEverything filters through this.\n\n## One obsessional goal\nGet all four apps to **version 1** — each with a proven happy path and the cross-app integrations working.\n(Onboarding VAs is downstream of this, not the goal.)\n\n## The bottleneck right now\n**Parallel v1 push across all four apps** — not a single front anymore. All four apps are live ([[BMH Institute]], [[Closer Lab]], [[Jitter]], [[Sandra]]). The work is finishing cross-app integrations and any reset browser-acceptance proof, driven concurrently rather than sequenced. [[Sandra]]\'s filter drawer — the old blocker — is shipped (PR #221, prod-verified). Live per-app fronts: see [[_Active]].\n\n## Operating mode\nThe objective is singular — four-app v1 — but execution is **parallel and autonomous**: many tasks across all four apps run concurrently. That\'s the whole point of this vault + the [[claude-codex-loop|orchestration loop]] (temporarily suspended 2026-06-01 — direct Claude Code sessions until repos are in known state; see [[2026-06-01 1645 — Clean-state reset before v1 repo work]]) — agents fan out and do work apparently autonomously, NOT one task at a time. "Focus" means the OBJECTIVE doesn\'t sprawl, not that work is serialized.\n- Tasks that advance v1 need no gate — fan them out.\n- Temporary gate (2026-06-01, per capture 1530): four-app repos were frozen until the BMH-OS hook/autonomy boundary was settled. **Resolved same day** — interfering global hooks rolled back, memory-bridge scripts cleaned up, boundary settled. Apps are unblocked; fan-out resumes.\n- The real guardrail is **additive / reversible / observable** (the infra enforces this), not permission-per-step.\n- A new SYSTEM (monorepo, AI-OS expansion, new tool) still waits unless it moves an app toward v1.\n\n## App status → v1\nSee [[MOC - v1]]. Quick read: [[BMH Institute]] live · [[Closer Lab]] live · [[Jitter]] live · [[Sandra]] live (remaining: [[BMH Institute]] → [[Sandra]] emit flow + [[Jitter]] final browser acceptance — Railway worker gate).\n\n## Deferred (recorded so we don\'t re-litigate)\n- **Monorepo migration** of the 4 apps — deferred; not required for integrations or v1. Plans: `~/Sites/BMH apps/bmh-platform-planning/`.\n- **Full 9-component AI OS** — deferred; this vault + the [[conventions|memory engine]] is the lean slice.\n\n### CURATED: _Active.md\n---\ntype: meta\nstatus: active\ncreated: 2026-05-31\nupdated: 2026-06-03\ntags: [v1]\nrelated: ["[[STRATEGY]]", "[[MOC - v1]]", "[[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]]", "[[Four-app v1 control ledger]]"]\n---\n# _Active — what now\n\nCurrent priorities, seeded from [[STRATEGY]]\'s bottleneck + the [[MOC - v1]] checklist. Frequently updated.\n\n## Operating model — Claude plans, Codex executes\n\n**Claude = planner/reviewer; Codex = executor.** For the four-app v1 push, Codex is executing the written per-app EXECUTE blocks directly in isolated worktrees; the start-orchestration bootstrap remains suspended until the repos are in known state. Claude still provides independent A5 review/approval before merge/deploy. Full handoff + recon + open decisions: [[2026-06-01 1815 — Four-app v1 plan + Codex execution handoff]]. Detailed per-app checklist: [[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]]. Cross-app context source: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]].\n\n**Autonomous = additive / reversible / observable** (STRATEGY\'s guardrail). A gate = destructive, irreversible, external-facing, or a judgment call.\n\n**Browser V1 acceptance gate:** fixture seeding, SQL assertions, unit/integration tests, GitHub Actions, and Playwright automation are scaffolding/supporting evidence only. Browser V1 is not accepted until Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution proves the persona flows through visible UI outcomes, screenshots, console/network inspection where relevant, and browser-console probes where required. Do not use Codex in-app browser / MAP / `iab` as the acceptance surface unless Jarrad explicitly reverses this.\n\n**Browser V1 UI-created data rule:** data setup is part of the browser test. For [[Closer Lab]] and [[BMH Institute]], create fixture/content/test records through Chrome/DevTools browser UI wherever the app UI supports creation or editing. Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth bootstrap when no signup/admin UI exists, and must be labeled as non-acceptance evidence.\n\n**2026-06-02 browser-surface correction:** Jarrad first reset [[Closer Lab]] and [[BMH Institute]] Browser V1 acceptance to zero, then superseded the MAP/in-app-browser requirement with Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution. Current controller evidence shows [[BMH Institute]] residual proof closed and [[Closer Lab]] Browser V1 markers closed for pre-read persistence, signed embed-token proof, and scoring/runtime; keep focus on [[Sandra]] unless a fresh specific gap appears.\n\n**2026-06-02 trust reset:** Jarrad challenged the controller\'s Playwright-heavy verification and does not trust acceptance unless it is revalidated in Chrome/DevTools. Treat Playwright/CI/API/DB evidence as support only. Fresh revalidation so far: [[BMH Institute]] Chrome snapshot/screenshot `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-current.*` visibly shows `Lesson complete`, with separate Sandra outcome confirmation `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-outcome.json`; [[Closer Lab]] member Chrome snapshot/screenshot `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-member-recording.*` visibly shows recording `72ad25d8-1b09-4ef9-a278-82113c12ce75`, `100%`, transcript, and rubric `MET 5 / 5`, with separate Sandra outcome support `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-sandra-outcome-support.json`. [[Jitter]] trust-reset browser work advanced in two steps: the earlier wrong-database/browser-auth mismatch was partially resolved by pinning production to the canonical `jitter-test` plane (`ypgntjjrrutjsratdwmk`) and proving controlled Chrome dialing in production, but that proof depended on a local scoped worker. Current blocker is no longer fixture creation; it is unattended production readiness. The remaining acceptance gap is a real worker path: Railway worker access/deploy is unresolved, browser execution intentionally does not run the product live-list executor, and `/api/mvp/session/executor` still requires a worker token for product live-list mode. Broader [[Sandra]] prior pass\n\n### CURATED: Home.md\n# Home — BMH OS\n\nThe control room. Start every session here.\n\n## North star\n[[STRATEGY]] — the one goal and the current bottleneck.\n\n## The v1 push\n[[MOC - v1]] — every app\'s checklist to version 1.\n\n## The three layers — where things live (read this if unsure)\nThe vault separates the *goal*, the *scoreboard*, and *today\'s work* into three files. They change at very different rates — don\'t confuse them:\n\n| File | Role | Changes |\n|------|------|---------|\n| [[STRATEGY]] | the **one goal + why** (north star) | almost never — only on milestone-done or a real pivot |\n| [[MOC - v1]] | the **scoreboard** — what "done" concretely means, as checkboxes | when a box gets ticked |\n| [[_Active]] | **what I\'m doing right now / next step** | every session |\n\nRule of thumb: each layer is a *map* of the one below it. STRATEGY → MOC (definition of done) → _Active (current step) → linked detail notes. A MOC is a **map, not a document** — it stays scannable and links *down* to detailed notes rather than holding the detail inline. If you\'re rewriting STRATEGY often, that churn probably belongs in _Active.\n\nPromotion: AI writes raw captures to `_inbox/`; **you** promote what matters into `projects/ decisions/ contracts/ sources/` (good friction). Nothing in those folders changes without your OK.\n\n## Apps\n- [[Sandra]] · CRM\n- [[Closer Lab]] · call practice\n- [[BMH Institute]] · LMS\n- [[Jitter]] · dialer\n\n## How this vault works\n[[conventions]] — the rules the AI follows when writing here.\nRaw AI captures land in `_inbox/`; you promote what matters (good friction).\n\n## Tooling\n[[skills]] — index of custom Claude Code skills (e.g. custom-codex-watcher) and how to invoke them.\n\n## Map — entry points\n- [[STRATEGY]] — the one goal + current bottleneck.\n- [[MOC - v1]] — every app\'s checklist to v1.\n- [[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]] — detailed per-app happy-path steps behind the MOC boxes.\n- [[_Active|Active priorities]] — what now.\n- [[_Active-Pairs|Active pairs]] — live Claude↔Codex orchestration registry.\n- Apps: [[Sandra]] · [[Closer Lab]] · [[BMH Institute]] · [[Jitter]].\n- [[skills]] — custom Claude Code skills index.\n- [[claude-codex-loop]] — autonomous execution loop.\n\n## Map — folders\n- `projects/` — promoted app & project notes.\n- `decisions/` — ADR-style decision records.\n- `contracts/` — agreed data shape two+ apps depend on (e.g. `call.completed`), written once so neither side drifts.\n- `sources/` — reference / extracted source material.\n- `mocs/` — Maps of Content.\n- `_inbox/` — AI write zone (raw per-session captures).\n- `_meta/` — conventions, tags, credentials, skills, capture daemon, briefing.\n- `_ai-context/` — AI-integration & orchestration docs.\n\n### CURATED: projects/BMH Institute.md\n---\ntype: project\nstatus: active\ntags: [lms, institute]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-02\nrelated: ["[[MOC - v1]]", "[[Sandra]]", "[[Closer Lab]]", "[[Four-app v1 control ledger]]", "[[2026-06-01 2233 — BMH Institute Browser V1 testing prompt]]"]\n---\n# BMH Institute\n\nTraining LMS for VAs. Next.js 16 + Supabase. **Live** at institute.bmhgroupkc.com (v1.1 shipped 2026-05-09).\n\n## v1 happy path\nInvite VA → set password → work assigned program → complete course → certificate.\n\n## Browser V1 fixture\n- Persistent browser testing prompt: [[2026-06-01 2233 — BMH Institute Browser V1 testing prompt]]\n- Control context: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]]\n- Acceptance surface is Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution with visible UI outcomes. Playwright/backend checks are supporting evidence only.\n- Browser V1 data creation must happen through the browser UI wherever the UI supports it. Create programs, courses, modules, lessons, content, quizzes, assignments, invites, submissions, and certificate-triggering flows through UI clicks instead of direct database population when possible.\n- Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth/persona bootstrap if no UI path exists. Existing database-seeded Browser V1 data may remain for Jarrad but does not count as acceptance unless equivalent UI-created flows are proven.\n- 2026-06-02 correction: acceptance surface superseded from in-app/MAP browser to Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution; controller residual proof closed in Chrome/DevTools after credential rotation.\n\n## Blockers to v1\n- Suspended-user login block shipped in PR #79; PR #79 merged 2026-06-02 with post-merge CI and Vercel green.\n- Certificate PDF never generated (`pdf_path` stays `pending`) — **deferred post-v1**.\n- Open engineering item: **Integration `course.completed` → [[Sandra]] not yet shipped** (emit side; Sandra receiver PR #228 merged 2026-06-02). See [[MOC - v1]] unchecked box.\n- Otherwise largely done; remaining non-code factor is founder confidence to run the pilot.\n\n## Integrations\n- Outbound → [[Sandra]]: `course.completed` updates contact training status.\n- Inbound ← [[Closer Lab]]: training/practice completion can enroll a course.\n\n## Auto-filed\n_AI-appended from inbox notes; prune freely._\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #80 (assignment-autocomplete-no-review) squash-merged to main; E2E lesson-completion trigger confirmed; PR #79 (suspended-login block) remains open draft. (source: [[2026-06-01 1838 — PR #80 merged; cleanup and optional verification (22e25ece)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — Suspended-login fix integrated on top of assignment fix (PR #79 skipped); E2E extended with quiz fail/unlock + HTML-print cert; 237 unit + 19 RTL + 13 integration + 4 Playwright all green; DRAFT PR pending final verify rerun. (source: [[2026-06-01 1959 — Institute v1 suspended-login fix + E2E proof (019e85cf)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 manual review found two P1 blockers: suspended users remain signed in on protected routes, and auto-approval doesn\'t validate assignmentId→lessonId binding; both block merge. (source: [[2026-06-01 2032 — PR #79 bmh-institute manual review findings (019e85e9)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 (suspended-login-block) passed all CI checks and is ready to merge; toggle draft=false to proceed. (source: [[2026-06-01 2120 — BMH Institute PR79 suspended-login-block A5 appr (60792029)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 (suspended-login-block) merged into bmh-institute main; post-merge CI and Vercel green, rollback tag recorded, lane closed. (source: [[2026-06-01 2121 — BMH Institute PR #79 merged, post-merge gates gr (019e860c)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 merged (head a737fac); E2E write-path rerun pending with explicit env mapping; branch drift and stale process blockers noted. (source: [[2026-06-01 2138 — Institute v1 executor respawn, PR#79 merged (019e862a)]])\n- 2026-06-02 — Handoff prompt to create persistent BMH Institute Browser V1 user-emulation fixture lab, including role group\n\n### CURATED: projects/Closer Lab.md\n---\ntype: project\nstatus: active\ntags: [practice, closer-lab]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-02\nrelated: ["[[MOC - v1]]", "[[Sandra]]", "[[BMH Institute]]", "[[Four-app v1 control ledger]]", "[[2026-06-02 — Closer Lab Browser V1 exhaustive testing prompt]]"]\n---\n# Closer Lab\n\nAI roleplay / call-practice. Next.js + Supabase, **live on Railway** (persistent WebSocket relay).\nEmbeds into [[BMH Institute]] via JWT iframe.\n\n- **Live URL (production, canonical):** https://web-production-a302.up.railway.app\n- Repo: `biginkc/closer-lab` · local: `$HOME/Sites/BMH apps/Closer Lab`\n- ⚠️ `closerlab.bmhgroup.com` (in `_archive/bmh-platform-monorepo-attempt/`) is a **dead/aspirational** domain from an abandoned monorepo — not live. Do not use.\n\n## v1 happy path\nLog in → run a roleplay scenario → get a score against the BMH playbook.\n\n## Browser V1 testing lab\n- Persistent browser testing prompt: [[2026-06-02 — Closer Lab Browser V1 exhaustive testing prompt]]\n- Control context: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]]\n- Acceptance surface is Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution with visible UI outcomes. GitHub Actions, Playwright, SQL, unit/integration/build checks, and fixture workflows are scaffolding only.\n- Browser V1 data creation must happen through the browser UI wherever the UI supports it. Create labs, roleplay attempts, scoring/rubric artifacts, share flows, and embed proofs through UI clicks instead of direct database population when possible.\n- Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth bootstrap if no UI path exists. Existing database-seeded Browser V1 data may remain for Jarrad but does not count as acceptance unless equivalent UI-created flows are proven.\n- 2026-06-02 correction: acceptance surface superseded from in-app/MAP browser to Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution; production Browser V1 markers are closed for pre-read persistence, BMH Institute signed embed-token path, and scoring/runtime.\n- 2026-06-02T07:14Z controller update: current acceptance surface is Chrome/DevTools real-browser evidence per Jarrad\'s later correction. Production owner/member UI-created Browser V1 data is in progress for `BROWSER-V1 CHROME Role Play 202606020640`. The Pre-read persistence marker is closed: admin Pre-read editor was corrected through the visible Chrome tab, saved with 142 chars and rendered preview, and member refresh showed the briefing plus `Start when ready`. Evidence: `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/23-owner-preread-clean-visible-before-save.txt`, `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/24-owner-preread-clean-saved.png`, `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/25-member-preread-visible-after-clean-save.png`, `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/25-member-preread-visible-after-clean-save.txt`. Remaining Browser V1 markers are signed embed-token proof and scoring proof with real learner speech or safe fixture transcript.\n- 2026-06-02T07:23Z controller update: signed embed-token proof is closed through the live [[BMH Institute]] production lesson path. The repo walkthrough lesson constant was stale and returned 404, but live learner navigation found `Embedded Practice Preview` at `/lessons/4d24fa5d-7191-4e50-ab3a-fdc456112c14`; BMH Institute minted the Closer iframe, Closer rendered `Closer Lab Demo: Skeptical Seller` with `Start when ready`, and clicking it entered the embedded runtime shell. Evidence: `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/28-institute-signed-closer-embed-ready.png`, `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/29-institute-signed-closer-embed-runtime-connecting.png`, `/tmp/closer-browser-v1-chrome/31-institute-embed-after-wait.png`. Remaining Browser V1 marker is scoring/runtime proof with real learner speech or safe fixture transcript.\n- 2026-06-02T08:05Z controller update: scoring/runtime marker is closed for the production Chrome/DevTools Browser V1 role play. The UI-created member recording `/recordings/72ad25d8-1b09-4ef9-a278-82113c12ce75` was first blocked by silen\n\n### CURATED: projects/Jitter.md\n---\ntype: project\nstatus: active\ntags: [dialer, jitter]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-03\nrelated: ["[[MOC - v1]]", "[[Sandra]]"]\n---\n# Jitter\n\nPredictive dialer. **Live** — placing real Twilio calls since 2026-05-19.\nCanonical dir: `~/Sites/BMH apps/Jitter` (renamed from the old `Jitter-POC`).\n\n## v1 happy path\nDial from a list → operator/AMD handling → disposition → recording.\n\n## Blockers to v1\n- Standalone Jitter v1 dial path is PASS after PR #144 live-canary proof.\n- [[Sandra]] writeback is functionally PASS after PR #145, Sandra receiver PR #224, and boundary fix PR #146: deployed production Jitter executor sent `sandra.writeback` to Sandra and created a production `call_activities` row.\n- CPS pacing is shipped: merged to `main` at `334ef8565d21b71bd3f645f05def2922179cee47` and deployed to production `dpl_75H8rsoMe7HEX7KSgtdo6cAjtJRS`.\n- Controlled production Chrome proof is only PARTIAL PASS: one `/dialer` run succeeded with browser audio connected and 4 successful `twilio.create_call` operations, but only while a local scoped worker was running.\n- Current blocker is unattended production readiness: Railway worker access/deploy is unresolved, so the final acceptance gate is one real-worker-backed Chrome proof, not more fixture/login repair.\n- Carrier reputation (~45% reject) — vendor problem, not engineering.\n\n## Integrations\n- Outbound → [[Sandra]]: emit `sandra.writeback`/terminal disposition (normalized call outcome, disposition, batch item, optional callback/recording metadata) → Sandra `call_activities`.\n\n## Known issues / notes\n- ⚠️ **Naming is inverted — footgun.** Supabase project `jitter-test` (`ypgntjjrrutjsratdwmk`) is the **REAL production** data plane; `jitter` (`sbidltfdktstzboivavv`) is **stale/dead**. Easy to nuke the wrong one — rename or document before anyone touches it.\n- Recording pipeline (PR #141) is **sound** — capture→enqueue→upload→hydrate→playback verified; recordings only created on *answered* calls. `K=3` dialing is correct.\n- **Recording happy path is queued behind Phase 7 batch validation** — once batch_id is issued and auth blockers resolved (Supabase Auth whitelist + Vercel log CLI), run a real predictive batch and verify answered calls produce recordings through to playback. Source: [[2026-05-31 0129 — Jitter dialing and recordings review (f6ae0a63)]]; superseded as immediate front by 2026-06-01 Phase 7 captures.\n\n## Auto-filed\n_AI-appended from inbox notes; prune freely._\n- 2026-05-31 — Twilio API key setup complete (Console UI only; REST fails); all 10 Jitter canary runtime values in 1Password; v3 key needs rotation to v4 due to screenshot exposure; canary unblocked. (source: [[2026-05-31 1713 — Twilio API Key setup + Jitter canary config (f04a4e07)]])\n- 2026-05-31 — Executor layer scaffolded (Hono, executor/ dir, 1,337 prospects in JSON); thin-slice goal is one hardcoded outbound Twilio call end-to-end before adding persistence, parallel waves, and Sandra integration. (source: [[2026-05-31 1714 — Executor scaffold + prospect data extraction (e2934f03)]])\n- 2026-05-31 — Closed provisioning gaps: all 9 Jitter dialer secrets now in 1P BMH Secrets vault; using Vercel URL for Twilio callbacks (custom domain lacks DNS); correct TwiML App SID confirmed; PRs #59 and #60 open. (source: [[2026-05-31 1730 — Jitter dialer provisioning gaps closed (240f7873)]])- 2026-05-31 — Jitter moved past POC to multi-line production: K-cap raised to 12, chunked 150-row batches proven, Wave 3 PSTN calls passed Lanes A–D; Lane E blocked on Twilio CPS access, Lane F blocked by UI race; MASTER-PLAN needs update. (source: [[2026-05-31 1731 — Jitter-POC multi-wave production status (b2d35a6a)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — Phase 7 predictive cockpit live on prod; awaiting operator batch_id and PR #155 fixture confirmation before first real predictive calls. (source: [[2026-06-01 1208 — Phase 7 predictive live, batch pending (0e94d78e)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — Round-1 predictive dialer testing blocked by Supabase auth rejecting\n\n### CURATED: projects/Sandra.md\n---\ntype: project\nstatus: active\ntags: [crm, sandra]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-03\naliases: [Sandra CRM]\nrelated: ["[[MOC - v1]]", "[[Jitter]]"]\n---\n# Sandra\n\nCRM for BMH. Next.js 16 + Supabase + Vercel. **Live** (~1,400 prospects).\nRepo: `~/Sites/BMH apps/Sandra`\n\n## v1 happy path\nImport prospects → filter to a target list → run an SMS/email sequence → handle replies.\n\n## Browser V1 exhaustive test pass\n- 2026-06-02 prompt handed to Nietzsche: execute `$HOME/BMH-OS/tmp/sandra-v1-test-plan-MERGED.md` as a real-browser Sandra/RCRM pass.\n- Method: drive a real browser like a human for route/persona/filter/write-path proof; read rendered UI, toasts, real console/network, and screenshots. Do not use Playwright/CLI/curl/scripts to exercise or assert features.\n- Narrow exceptions: data plumbing only for 10 browser users, `SANDRA-BROWSER-V1` / `PROD-CANARY` rows, DB-oracle filter counts, and `resetTenantTables()` teardown; authorization probes run from browser DevTools console against the live logged-in session.\n- Deliverable: `$HOME/BMH-OS/tmp/sandra-v1-test-RESULTS.md` with 1Password refs only, browser-backed matrices, redacted provider ledger, cleanup status, defects, and verdict.\n- 2026-06-02T08:23Z controller-owned Chrome update: >250-row UI-created import/job marker is closed. Admin Owner used Chrome/DevTools to select Add Data, upload `/private/tmp/sandra-browser-v1-import-260.csv`, select DealMachine/Jackson County MO, review `260 of 260` valid rows, start the durable job without SMS/provider send, and verify job `/jobs/bbc09186-0d2d-4250-be8b-356d14d94e28` completed `260/260` with `260` succeeded, `0` failed, `0` skipped. Evidence: `/private/tmp/sandra-v1-browser-evidence/059-*` through `071-*`. Overall Browser V1 verdict remains PARTIAL pending filter/persona/mobile/realtime/reset matrix.\n- 2026-06-02T08:43Z controller-owned Chrome update: No Membership and Cross Org visibility slices are closed. No Membership auth fixture was repaired through approved service-role setup, then dashboard/properties/leads/messages rendered zero/empty states with no imported BMH rows. Cross Org dashboard/properties rendered zero/empty states after the merge RPC fix. A no-org Quick Filters UI defect was found and patched in `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/_components/quick-filters-bar.tsx`; no-org `/properties` now renders empty prospects without `Failed to load Quick Filters`; `npm run typecheck -- --pretty false` passed. Overall Browser V1 remains PARTIAL pending filter matrix, write-path/realtime/mobile/reset slices and merge/deploy of the no-org fix.\n- 2026-06-02T08:53Z controller code/PR update: no-org Quick Filters fix was isolated on fresh branch `codex/sandra-no-org-quickfilters`, verified with `npm run typecheck -- --pretty false`, `npm run verify`, and Husky pre-commit `npm run verify`, then merged as PR #223. Remote checks passed: Playwright golden paths `26808897046`, Vercel preview, and Vercel Preview Comments. Squash merge `295b9a17fb458d502ddf417dc1b116b9ca22d1c6`; remote feature branch deleted. No-org Quick Filters marker is closed in code; Browser V1 remains PARTIAL pending filter matrix, write-path/realtime/mobile/reset, and cleanup proof.\n- 2026-06-02T09:07Z controller watchdog update: Hooke completed non-browser prep for the next Admin Owner `/properties` filter visual/DB-oracle slice. Controller remediated the local server blocker by restarting Sandra on `localhost:3457` in detached screen session `sandra-v1-dev-3457` with the existing test env mapped to the middleware\'s expected public Supabase env names; `/properties` now returns a login redirect instead of 500. Browser V1 remains PARTIAL pending controller-owned Chrome login/navigation for filter matrix evidence `088-*` through `095-*`, then write-path/realtime/mobile/reset slices.\n- 2026-06-02T09:14Z controller-owned Chrome update: Admin Owner `/properties` filter visual/DB-oracle slice completed. Evidence `088-*` through `094-*` plus\n\n### CURATED: mocs/MOC - v1 Verification Steps.md\n---\ntype: moc\nstatus: active\ntags: [v1, sandra, jitter, closer-lab, institute]\ncreated: 2026-06-01\nupdated: 2026-06-03\nrelated: ["[[MOC - v1]]", "[[_Active]]", "[[Sandra]]", "[[Jitter]]", "[[Closer Lab]]", "[[BMH Institute]]"]\n---\n# MOC - v1 Verification Steps\n\nDetailed happy-path **+ negative + edge** checklists — the step-by-step detail behind [[MOC - v1]]\'s boxes. The MOC is the scoreboard (one box per app); this is the browser-by-browser expansion. Tick a box when that step passes (`PASS` / `FAIL` / `BLOCKED` / `UNTESTED`).\n\n**Each app section is grouped by dimension:** 1) golden path, 2) auth/role boundaries, 3) bad input, 4) provider failures, 5) duplicate/replay, 6) concurrency/races, 7) empty/limit states, 8) interruptions, 9) integrity/flow-specific, 10+) cleanup. Steps are grounded in the actual codebase (file/route citations); `(UNKNOWN …)` marks where code didn\'t reveal the answer — those are themselves things to verify.\n\n**Principle:** agents map *where to look*; Browser V1 acceptance proves *what works for a VA* through Chrome/DevTools real-browser clicks/navigation and visible UI outcomes. Browser V1 data creation is also part of the browser proof: create the fixture/content/test records through Chrome wherever the UI supports creation or editing. Playwright automation, SQL, shell, unit/integration tests, GitHub Actions, and direct database/API population are supporting evidence only; they do not satisfy Browser V1 acceptance by themselves.\n\nSource: parallel read-only recon agents (2026-06-01) over each repo at `~/Sites/BMH apps/`; original capture [[2026-06-01 1653 — Four-app v1 browser verification approach]].\n\n> ⚠️ **Recon flagged real v1 risks** (verify before calling done): Jitter\'s **Sandra writeback is stubbed/skipped** (observed in audit, not POSTed). **Institute** never generates a certificate PDF (`pdf_path` stays `\'pending\'`) and cert PDF remains deferred post-v1. Resolved since recon: Jitter auth/role model shipped in PR #144; Institute suspended-login block shipped in PR #79; Jitter Sandra writeback shipped in PRs #145/#146 (Jitter) + PR #224 (Sandra), production executor proof PASS 2026-06-02. See the relevant app sections.\n\n## Recon first (read-only, per app)\n- [ ] **One code-review agent per app:** map v1 features → actual routes/components/API endpoints/tests/env vars.\n- [ ] **One integration-contract agent:** compare [[Jitter]]→[[Sandra]] and [[BMH Institute]]→[[Closer Lab]] payload/auth/origin expectations.\n- [ ] **One QA-\n\n### CURATED: mocs/MOC - v1.md\n---\ntype: moc\nstatus: active\ntags: [v1]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-03\n---\n# MOC - v1\n\nDefinition of done = every box checked. Filtered by [[STRATEGY]]. Step-by-step detail behind each happy-path box → [[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]].\n\n## [[Sandra]] (CRM) — live\n- [x] Validate /properties filters on prod data — SHIPPED 2026-05-31 (PR #221, `8b9b238`): relationship-filter bugs fixed, Pass 1 272/272 + deployed-prod Pass 2 100/100. See [[Sandra Filter Fix Loop]].\n- [x] Happy path: import → filter prospects → run sequence → reply handled — PR #222 merged 2026-06-02; prod canaries and post-merge E2E `26797451702` passed\n- [x] Integration: receive [[Jitter]] writeback → log `call_activities` — [[Sandra]] PR #224 merged; production executor proof PASS 2026-06-02\n\n## [[Closer Lab]] — live\n- [x] Ship PR #60 — merged 2026-06-02; PR #61 already closed — superseded by PR #62\n- [x] Happy path: log in → run roleplay → get score — PR #60 merged 2026-06-02; post-fix main E2E and production smoke passed\n- [x] Integration: emit practice/call outcome → [[Sandra]] — PRs #71/#72 ([[Closer Lab]]) + PR #225 ([[Sandra]]) merged; production proof PASS 2026-06-02\n\n## [[BMH Institute]] — live\n- [x] Happy path: invite → learn → complete course — PR #79 merged 2026-06-02; seeded Playwright E2E green; cert PDF deferred post-v1\n- [ ] Integration: `course.completed` → [[Sandra]] contact\n\n## [[Jitter]] (dialer) — live\n- [x] Happy path: dial → disposition → recording — PR #144 merged 2026-06-02; capped live canary passed and CPS pacing is now merged/deployed through `334ef85`\n- [x] Integration: wire [[Sandra]] writeback — shipped in Sandra PR #145, Sandra PR #224, and Jitter boundary fix PR #146; deployed production executor proof wrote to Sandra `call_activities` on 2026-06-02\n- [x] v1 hardening: add auth/role model — PR #144 merged 2026-06-02 with Supabase auth, middleware, role RLS, and public webhook/executor exceptions\n- [ ] Final browser acceptance: rerun `/dialer` in Chrome with the real production worker — controlled Chrome proof succeeded with a local scoped worker, but unattended worker readiness is still the remaining gate\n\n### CURATED: _ai-context/CLAUDE-Setup.md\n---\ntype: meta\nstatus: active\ncreated: 2026-05-31\nupdated: 2026-05-31\ntags: [ai-os]\nrelated: ["[[Home]]", "[[conventions]]", "[[claude-codex-loop]]"]\n---\n# CLAUDE Setup — how the vault ↔ Claude integration works\n\nCompanion doc for the BMH-OS ↔ Claude Code wiring. Explains where memory lives, how every Claude tab boots with vault context, how to test the wiring, and how to keep it healthy. If you only read one thing: **the vault is the source of truth; everything else points into it.**\n\n## Canonical-memory model\n\n`~/BMH-OS` is the **single source of truth** for durable cross-session memory. Two other surfaces look like memory but are not — they are thin **pointers** into the vault:\n\n- The per-project auto-memory at `~/.claude/projects/<project>/memory/MEMORY.md` — an index of one-line pointers, not the content itself.\n- The SessionStart **briefing** injected into every tab (see below) — pointers + status lines, never note bodies.\n\n**On any conflict, the vault wins.** A pointer that disagrees with the vault is stale; fix the pointer, trust the vault. This keeps a single write target: durable facts get promoted into `projects/ decisions/ contracts/ sources/` per [[conventions]], and the pointers are regenerated/refreshed to match — never the other way around.\n\n## How context loads in every tab\n\nTwo mechanisms, complementary:\n\n1. **SessionStart hook → briefing.** On every new Claude tab (any working directory), the SessionStart hook runs `~/BMH-OS/_meta/session-briefing.sh`. It emits a **lean** briefing assembled live from the vault:\n   - **Goal** and **Bottleneck** pulled from `STRATEGY.md` (the "One obsessional goal" and "The bottleneck right now" sections).\n   - **Active now:** the first few `- ` items from `_Active.md`.\n   - **Projects:** each note in `projects/` with its `status:`.\n   - **Recent captures:** the 4 newest `_inbox/*.md` titles.\n   The script is **fail-soft** (`set -uo pipefail`, exits 0 if the vault is missing) so a broken vault never blocks a session. It drains and ignores the hook JSON on stdin.\n\n2. **Root `CLAUDE.md` auto-load (vault cwd only).** When a Claude session\'s working directory is the vault (`~/BMH-OS`), Claude Code auto-loads the root `CLAUDE.md` in full — the complete protocol. Outside the vault you get the lean briefing instead, which points you back to `~/BMH-OS/CLAUDE.md` if you need the full protocol.\n\nThe division is deliberate: the briefing is the **everywhere, lightweight** signal; the full `CLAUDE.md` is the **in-vault\n\n### CURATED: _ai-context/claude-codex-loop.md\n---\ntype: meta\nstatus: active\ncreated: 2026-05-31\nupdated: 2026-05-31\ntags: [ai-os]\nrelated: ["[[_Active-Pairs]]", "[[STRATEGY]]", "[[CLAUDE-Setup]]"]\n---\n# Claude ↔ Codex convergence loop\n\nThe formal protocol for the autonomous, adversarial Claude↔Codex loop. Claude **plans, reviews, and independently verifies**; Codex **executes everything** with hands on the computer. The loop cycles until the goal is proven complete or a real blocker stops it. Referencing Codex here is correct — it is the subject of this protocol.\n\nCanonical source: the Codex skill `~/.codex/skills/custom-convergence-loop/SKILL.md`. This note formalizes it for the vault and names the BMH-OS conventions (pairing, handoff blocks, loop history) layered on top.\n\n## Roles\n\n- **Claude = brain / orchestrator / reviewer / bridge-driver.** Plans the goal, defines acceptance gates, reviews every Codex report, and **independently verifies** with its own tools (reads files, runs checks, opens the browser) rather than trusting Codex\'s word. Claude holds the merge gate. Claude also **drives the handoff bridge** — it delivers each EXECUTE into Codex and pulls the REPORT back (via `custom-codex-watcher`; see Transport). Claude is advisory on *what* to do; it is authoritative on *whether it\'s done*.\n- **Codex = executor / hands.** Does all **task** actuation — file edits, commands, git, browser proof — for the work itself. (The cross-app *handoff* is driven by Claude, not Codex — see Transport.) Codex **adversarially refutes** each instruction before executing it.\n\nClaude is not the first reviewer of Codex\'s code: once a diff exists, Codex runs `custom-manual-code-review` (with reviewer sub-agents) and fixes valid findings **before** escalating to Claude for review or a next-step decision.\n\n## Entry — Claude-initiated\n\nJarrad kicks the loop off from the Claude side by running the Claude skill **`custom-start-orchestration`** (the renamed + extended kickoff). That skill:\n\n1. Plans the goal and maps it to a `plan_source` (repo plan / roadmap / issue / PR / thread).\n2. Defines a stable **`goal_id`** and explicit, independently verifiable **acceptance gates**.\n3. Registers the **paired sessions** (see Pairing) in [[_Active-Pairs]].\n4. Emits the first **EXECUTE** handoff block to Codex.\n\nIf acceptance gates are missing, derive a conservative gate list from the goal and confirm it before accepting any `DONE`.\n\n## Pairing & naming\n\nEach loop runs as a 1:1 pair of sessions, titled by `goal_id` with a role suff\n\n### CURATED: _ai-context/research-memory-and-model-specificity.md\n---\ntype: source\nstatus: active\ncreated: 2026-05-31\nupdated: 2026-05-31\ntags: [ai-os]\nrelated: ["[[CLAUDE-Setup]]"]\n---\n# Research: Memory architecture & Claude model specificity\n\nOngoing research area. Two themes that govern how the AI OS *remembers* and\n*which brain* it uses. Not live web research — this note defines the area and\nparks open threads as **Question / Idea / Status (open)**. Setup state lives in\n[[CLAUDE-Setup]].\n\n---\n\n## Theme A — Memory architecture\n\nThere are several distinct memory layers in play. They are easy to conflate,\nand conflating them is how notes get duplicated and contradict each other. The\nresearch goal is to keep their *roles* crisp and make the vault the single\ncanonical store.\n\n### The layers\n\n1. **`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — global behavior.** How Claude *acts* across every\n   project: response format, pushback stance, worktree hygiene, model-switch\n   nudges. Behavioral policy, not facts about the business. Hand-authored,\n   rarely auto-written.\n2. **`~/.claude/projects/.../MEMORY.md` (+ linked notes) — auto-memory.** A\n   per-project index of durable facts/decisions the assistant accumulates\n   (app-launch status, the filter-fix loop, the memory daemon). Convenient and\n   close to the runtime, but it is *Claude-runtime-local* — not the canonical\n   business store, and not visible to Codex or other tools.\n3. **`~/BMH-OS` vault — canonical store.** The durable, tool-agnostic source of\n   truth: projects, decisions, contracts, sources, MOCs, under [[conventions]].\n   Linked markdown, no Dataview. This is what *should* win when layers disagree.\n4. **SessionStart hooks — the bridge.** Inject vault context into a fresh Claude\n   session at startup (see [[CLAUDE-Setup]] and the briefing-tuning thread in\n   [[research-vault-integration]]). The hook is plumbing, not storage — it\n   *carries* memory from the vault into context; it doesn\'t *hold* it.\n\n### How they relate (the canonical-vault model)\n\n- **Behavior** lives in `CLAUDE.md` (layer 1).\n- **Facts/decisions** belong in the **vault** (layer 3) — canonical.\n- **Auto-memory** (layer 2) is a fast scratch/cache close to the Claude runtime;\n  anything durable there should be *promoted* into the vault, not left as the\n  authority.\n- **Hooks** (layer 4) move layer-3 content into a session; they should read from\n  the vault, never become a parallel store.\n\n**Question.** Where is the boundary between auto-memory (layer 2) and the vault\n(layer 3)? When does an auto-memory fact graduate t\n\n### CURATED: _ai-context/research-vault-integration.md\n---\ntype: source\nstatus: active\ncreated: 2026-05-31\nupdated: 2026-05-31\ntags: [ai-os]\nrelated: ["[[CLAUDE-Setup]]", "[[claude-codex-loop]]"]\n---\n# Research: Vault ↔ Claude integration\n\nOngoing research area. Open questions and directions for deepening how the\n`~/BMH-OS` vault feeds Claude (and Codex) and how Claude writes back. Not live\nweb research — this note *defines* the area and parks open threads. Each entry\nis **Question / Idea / Status (open)**. Setup state lives in [[CLAUDE-Setup]];\nthe autonomous wake loop lives in [[claude-codex-loop]].\n\n## 1. MCP bundles for vault access\n\n**Question.** Should vault reads/writes go through a dedicated MCP server\n(filesystem-scoped to `~/BMH-OS`, or an Obsidian-specific MCP) instead of raw\n`Read`/`Write`/`Bash`? What does an MCP buy us that file tools don\'t — link\ngraph queries, tag-aware search, frontmatter validation, orphan detection at\nwrite time?\n\n**Idea.** A thin "vault MCP" exposing a small verb set: `search(query, tag?)`,\n`get(note)`, `backlinks(note)`, `write(note, frontmatter, body)` with the\n[[conventions]] orphan-gate + tag-lint enforced server-side so no agent can\nwrite an invalid note. Could wrap the existing `_meta/tag-lint.py`. Evaluate\nthe community Obsidian MCP servers vs. a purpose-built one before committing.\n\n**Status (open).** No vault MCP today; agents use plain file tools. Decide:\nadopt existing MCP, build thin custom, or stay on file tools and lean on\nconventions + lint as the guardrail.\n\n## 2. Tuning the SessionStart briefing\n\n**Question.** What belongs in the SessionStart hook injection, and what should\nbe pulled on demand instead? The briefing must stay lean as the vault grows —\na hook that dumps the whole vault defeats itself.\n\n**Idea.** Tier the briefing: (a) always inject — `Home.md`, `_Active.md`,\ncurrent strategy pointer, the convention/tag rules; (b) inject a *manifest*\n(titles + one-line summaries + paths) rather than full note bodies, so Claude\nknows what exists and fetches the body only when relevant; (c) never inject —\narchived notes, raw `_inbox/` captures, session logs. Watch the token budget\nof the hook output as a first-class metric; set a ceiling and alert when the\nmanifest approaches it.\n\n**Status (open).** Briefing exists (see [[CLAUDE-Setup]]); no formal tiering or\ntoken ceiling yet. Open: define the manifest format and the inject/exclude\nrules as the vault scales past a few dozen notes.\n\n## 3. Surviving context compaction\n\n**Question.** When a long session compacts,\n\n### DECISION/CLI-over-GUI wake plane mailbox architecture.md\n---\ntype: decision\nstatus: active\ntags: [session, auto-capture]\ncreated: 2026-06-01\nupdated: 2026-06-01\nrelated: ["[[STRATEGY]]", "[[Home]]"]\n---\n# 2026-06-01 1514 — GUI routing safety architecture (032a66d9)\n\nAuto-captured from Claude Code session `032a66d9-c9b1-42d8-afea-750a8c8e61c3`. Promote anything important into a real note.\n\n## Decisions\n- Split Claude<->Codex into data plane (file mailbox\n\n### DECISION/Claude orchestrates Codex executes manual paste transport.md\n---\ntype: decision\nstatus: active\ntags: [session, auto-capture]\ncreated: 2026-0