6 2123 — Doc-driven Jitter B2 plan with sub-agents (019e9fd7)]].\n- Carrier reputation (~45% reject) — vendor problem, not engineering.\n- **Current engineering front: Telnyx provider seam.** Twilio account suspended (KYC), so the\n  carrier is being swapped. A provider-abstraction layer is built and reconciled to Telnyx\'s\n  real API shapes — Phases A/B (seam + Telnyx backend + browser operator), R (schema\n  reconciliation: AMD `machine`, CallSid-from-webhook, 16-route build fix), C0 (exhaustive\n  tests) — on branch `codex/jitter-provider-abstraction`, `next build` green, 1092 unit tests.\n  Live validation PASSED 2026-06-04; current gate is the B2 trust-boundary/readiness/single-line dial order, then Railway worker proof.\n- **New official-docs-first finish-out plan:** [[2026-06-06 2123 — Doc-driven Jitter B2 plan with sub-agents (019e9fd7)]]. Immediate implication: the current failing operator TeXML auth test may be enforcing callback-style signature rules on the wrong boundary. The order is now trust-boundary fix first, then browser-audio readiness contract, then single-line live dial, then real Railway worker proof.\n\n## Integrations\n- Outbound → [[Sandra]]: emit `sandra.writeback`/terminal disposition (normalized call outcome, disposition, batch item, optional callback/recording metadata) → Sandra `call_activities`.\n\n## Known issues / notes\n- ⚠️ **Naming is inverted — footgun.** Supabase project `jitter-test` (`ypgntjjrrutjsratdwmk`) is the **REAL production** data plane; `jitter` (`sbidltfdktstzboivavv`) is **stale/dead**. Easy to nuke the wrong one — rename or document before anyone touches it.\n- Recording pipeline (PR #141) is **sound** — capture→enqueue→upload→hydrate→playback verified; recordings only created on *answered* calls. `K=3` dialing is correct.\n- **Recording happy path is queued behind Phase 7 batch validation** — once batch_id is issued and auth blockers resolved (Supabase Auth whitelist + Vercel log CLI), run a real predictive batch