t drift; drift is when the curated claim is actually WRONG or OUT OF DATE now. When in doubt, omit it. Prefer zero findings over a noisy one — false alarms train the reader to ignore this list.\n\nReply with ONLY a JSON object (no prose, no code fence):\n  {"contradictions": [ {"severity": "high|med", "source": "<curated file that is wrong, e.g. _Active.md>", "claim": "<the stale/contradicted claim, short>", "superseded_by": "<what reality now says + which capture/note shows it>", "fix": "<one-line concrete edit to the source file>"} ] }\nEmpty array if nothing is genuinely wrong.\n\n--- VAULT ---\n### CURATED: STRATEGY.md\n---\ntype: source\nstatus: active\ntags: [strategy]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-07\n---\n# STRATEGY — the brain\n\nEverything filters through this.\n\n## One obsessional goal\nGet all four apps to **version 1** — each with a proven happy path and the cross-app integrations working.\n(Onboarding VAs is downstream of this, not the goal.)\n\n## The bottleneck right now\n**Parallel v1 push across all four apps** — not a single front anymore. All four apps are live ([[BMH Institute]], [[Closer Lab]], [[Jitter]], [[Sandra]]). The work is finishing cross-app integrations and any reset browser-acceptance proof, driven concurrently rather than sequenced. [[Sandra]]\'s filter drawer — the old blocker — is shipped (PR #221, prod-verified). Live per-app fronts: see [[_Active]].\n\n## Operating mode\nThe objective is singular — four-app v1 — but execution is **parallel and autonomous**: many tasks across all four apps run concurrently. That\'s the whole point of this vault + the [[claude-codex-loop|orchestration loop]] (temporarily suspended 2026-06-01 — direct Claude Code sessions until repos are in known state; see [[2026-06-01 1645 — Clean-state reset before v1 repo work]]) — agents fan out and do work apparently autonomously, NOT one task at a time. "Focus" means the OBJECTIVE doesn\'t sprawl, not that work is serialized.\n- Tasks that advance v1 need no gate — fan them out.\n- Temporary gate (2026-06-01, per capture 1530): four-app repos were frozen until the BMH-OS hook/autonomy boundary was settled. **Resolved same day** — interfering global hooks rolled back, memory-bridge scripts cleaned up, boundary settled. Apps are unblocked; fan-out resumes.\n- The real guardrail is **additive / reversible / observable** (the infra enforces this), not permission-per-step.\n- A new SYSTEM (monorepo, AI-OS expansion, new tool) still waits unless it moves an app toward v1.\n\n## App status → v1\nSee [[MOC - v1]]. Quick read: [[BMH Institute]] live · [[Closer Lab]] live · [[Jitter]] live · [[Sandra]] live (remaining: [[BMH Institute]] → [[Sandra]] emit flow + [[Jitter]] final browser acceptance — trust-boundary fix → browser-audio readiness contract → single-line live Telnyx dial proof → Railway worker-backed unattended proof (B2 plan, 2026-06-06)).\n\n## Deferred (recorded so we don\'t re-litigate)\n- **Monorepo migration** of the 4 apps — deferred; not required for integrations or v1. Plans: `~/Sites/BMH apps/bmh-platform-planning/`.\n- **Full 9-component AI OS** — deferred; this vault + the [[conventions|memory engine]] is the lean slice.\n\n### CURATED: _Active.md\n---\ntype: meta\nstatus: active\ncreated: 2026-05-31\nupdated: 2026-06-07\ntags: [v1]\nrelated: ["[[STRATEGY]]", "[[MOC - v1]]", "[[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]]", "[[Four-app v1 control ledger]]"]\n---\n# _Active — what now\n\nCurrent priorities, seeded from [[STRATEGY]]\'s bottleneck + the [[MOC - v1]] checklist. Frequently updated.\n\n## Operating model — Claude plans, Codex executes\n\n**Claude = planner/reviewer; Codex = executor.** For the four-app v1 push, Codex is executing the written per-app EXECUTE blocks directly in isolated worktrees; the start-orchestration bootstrap remains suspended until the repos are in known state. Claude still provides independent A5 review/approval before merge/deploy. Full handoff + recon + open decisions: [[2026-06-01 1815 — Four-app v1 plan + Codex execution handoff]]. Detailed per-app checklist: [[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]]. Cross-app context source: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]].\n\n**Autonomous = additive / reversible / observable** (STRATEGY\'s guardrail). A gate = destructive, irreversible, external-facing, or a judgment call.\n\n**Browser V1 acceptance gate:** fixture seeding, SQL assertions, unit/integration tests, GitHub Actions, and Playwright automation are scaffolding/supporting evidence only. Browser V1 is not accepted until Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution proves the persona flows through visible UI outcomes, screenshots, console/network inspection where relevant, and browser-console probes where required. Do not use Codex in-app browser / MAP / `iab` as the acceptance surface unless Jarrad explicitly reverses this.\n\n**Browser V1 UI-created data rule:** data setup is part of the browser test. For [[Closer Lab]] and [[BMH Institute]], create fixture/content/test records through Chrome/DevTools browser UI wherever the app UI supports creation or editing. Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth bootstrap when no signup/admin UI exists, and must be labeled as non-acceptance evidence.\n\n**2026-06-02 browser-surface correction:** Jarrad first reset [[Closer Lab]] and [[BMH Institute]] Browser V1 acceptance to zero, then superseded the MAP/in-app-browser requirement with Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution. Current controller evidence shows [[BMH Institute]] residual proof closed and [[Closer Lab]] Browser V1 markers closed for pre-read persistence, signed embed-token proof, and scoring/runtime; keep focus on [[Sandra]] unless a fresh specific gap appears.\n\n**2026-06-02 trust reset:** Jarrad challenged the controller\'s Playwright-heavy verification and does not trust acceptance unless it is revalidated in Chrome/DevTools. Treat Playwright/CI/API/DB evidence as support only. Fresh revalidation so far: [[BMH Institute]] Chrome snapshot/screenshot `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-current.*` visibly shows `Lesson complete`, with separate Sandra outcome confirmation `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-outcome.json`; [[Closer Lab]] member Chrome snapshot/screenshot `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-member-recording.*` visibly shows recording `72ad25d8-1b09-4ef9-a278-82113c12ce75`, `100%`, transcript, and rubric `MET 5 / 5`, with separate Sandra outcome support `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-sandra-outcome-support.json`. [[Jitter]] trust-reset browser work advanced in two steps: the earlier wrong-database/browser-auth mismatch was partially resolved by pinning production to the canonical `jitter-test` plane (`ypgntjjrrutjsratdwmk`) and proving controlled Chrome dialing in production, but that proof depended on a local scoped worker. Current blocker is no longer fixture creation; it is the **carrier swap**: Twilio is KYC-suspended/retired and **Telnyx is now the active carrier (account fully verified) — carrier validation PASSED 2026-06-04** — that carrier validation precedes the worker gate. The current Jitter gate (B2 plan, 2026-06-06) is **trust-boundary fix → browser-audio readiness contract → single-l\n\n### CURATED: Home.md\n# Home — BMH OS\n\nThe control room. Start every session here.\n\n## North star\n[[STRATEGY]] — the one goal and the current bottleneck.\n\n## The v1 push\n[[MOC - v1]] — every app\'s checklist to version 1.\n\n## The three layers — where things live (read this if unsure)\nThe vault separates the *goal*, the *scoreboard*, and *today\'s work* into three files. They change at very different rates — don\'t confuse them:\n\n| File | Role | Changes |\n|------|------|---------|\n| [[STRATEGY]] | the **one goal + why** (north star) | almost never — only on milestone-done or a real pivot |\n| [[MOC - v1]] | the **scoreboard** — what "done" concretely means, as checkboxes | when a box gets ticked |\n| [[_Active]] | **what I\'m doing right now / next step** | every session |\n\nRule of thumb: each layer is a *map* of the one below it. STRATEGY → MOC (definition of done) → _Active (current step) → linked detail notes. A MOC is a **map, not a document** — it stays scannable and links *down* to detailed notes rather than holding the detail inline. If you\'re rewriting STRATEGY often, that churn probably belongs in _Active.\n\nPromotion: AI writes raw captures to `_inbox/`; **you** promote what matters into `projects/ decisions/ contracts/ sources/` (good friction). Nothing in those folders changes without your OK.\n\n## Apps\n- [[Sandra]] · CRM\n- [[Closer Lab]] · call practice\n- [[BMH Institute]] · LMS\n- [[Jitter]] · dialer\n\n## Content\n- [[BMH Training Course]] · 19-module onboarding course (feeds [[BMH Institute]])\n\n## How this vault works\n[[conventions]] — the rules the AI follows when writing here.\nRaw AI captures land in `_inbox/`; you promote what matters (good friction).\n\n## Tooling\n[[skills]] — index of custom Claude Code skills (e.g. custom-codex-watcher) and how to invoke them.\n\n## Map — entry points\n- [[STRATEGY]] — the one goal + current bottleneck.\n- [[MOC - v1]] — every app\'s checklist to v1.\n- [[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]] — detailed per-app happy-path steps behind the MOC boxes.\n- [[_Active|Active priorities]] — what now.\n- [[_Active-Pairs|Active pairs]] — live Claude↔Codex orchestration registry.\n- Apps: [[Sandra]] · [[Closer Lab]] · [[BMH Institute]] · [[Jitter]].\n- [[skills]] — custom Claude Code skills index.\n- [[claude-codex-loop]] — autonomous execution loop.\n\n## Map — folders\n- `projects/` — promoted app & project notes.\n- `decisions/` — ADR-style decision records.\n- `contracts/` — agreed data shape two+ apps depend on (e.g. `call.completed`), written once so neither side drifts.\n- `sources/` — reference / extracted source material.\n- `mocs/` — Maps of Content.\n- `_inbox/` — AI write zone (raw per-session captures).\n- `_meta/` — conventions, tags, credentials, skills, capture daemon, briefing.\n- `_ai-context/` — AI-integration & orchestration docs.\n\n### CURATED: projects/BMH Institute.md\n---\ntype: project\nstatus: active\ntags: [lms, institute]\ncreated: 2026-05-30\nupdated: 2026-06-02\nrelated: ["[[MOC - v1]]", "[[Sandra]]", "[[Closer Lab]]", "[[Four-app v1 control ledger]]", "[[2026-06-01 2233 — BMH Institute Browser V1 testing prompt]]"]\n---\n# BMH Institute\n\nTraining LMS for VAs. Next.js 16 + Supabase. **Live** at institute.bmhgroupkc.com (v1.1 shipped 2026-05-09).\n\n## v1 happy path\nInvite VA → set password → work assigned program → complete course → certificate.\n\n## Browser V1 fixture\n- Persistent browser testing prompt: [[2026-06-01 2233 — BMH Institute Browser V1 testing prompt]]\n- Control context: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]]\n- Acceptance surface is Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution with visible UI outcomes. Playwright/backend checks are supporting evidence only.\n- Browser V1 data creation must happen through the browser UI wherever the UI supports it. Create programs, courses, modules, lessons, content, quizzes, assignments, invites, submissions, and certificate-triggering flows through UI clicks instead of direct database population when possible.\n- Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth/persona bootstrap if no UI path exists. Existing database-seeded Browser V1 data may remain for Jarrad but does not count as acceptance unless equivalent UI-created flows are proven.\n- 2026-06-02 correction: acceptance surface superseded from in-app/MAP browser to Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution; controller residual proof closed in Chrome/DevTools after credential rotation.\n\n## Blockers to v1\n- Suspended-user login block shipped in PR #79; PR #79 merged 2026-06-02 with post-merge CI and Vercel green.\n- Certificate PDF never generated (`pdf_path` stays `pending`) — **deferred post-v1**.\n- Open engineering item: **Integration `course.completed` → [[Sandra]] not yet shipped** (emit side; Sandra receiver PR #228 merged 2026-06-02). See [[MOC - v1]] unchecked box.\n- Otherwise largely done; remaining non-code factor is founder confidence to run the pilot.\n\n## Integrations\n- Outbound → [[Sandra]]: `course.completed` updates contact training status.\n- Inbound ← [[Closer Lab]]: training/practice completion can enroll a course.\n\n## Auto-filed\n_AI-appended from inbox notes; prune freely._\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #80 (assignment-autocomplete-no-review) squash-merged to main; E2E lesson-completion trigger confirmed; PR #79 (suspended-login block) remains open draft. (source: [[2026-06-01 1838 — PR #80 merged; cleanup and optional verification (22e25ece)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — Suspended-login fix integrated on top of assignment fix (PR #79 skipped); E2E extended with quiz fail/unlock + HTML-print cert; 237 unit + 19 RTL + 13 integration + 4 Playwright all green; DRAFT PR pending final verify rerun. (source: [[2026-06-01 1959 — Institute v1 suspended-login fix + E2E proof (019e85cf)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 manual review found two P1 blockers: suspended users remain signed in on protected routes, and auto-approval doesn\'t validate assignmentId→lessonId binding; both block merge. (source: [[2026-06-01 2032 — PR #79 bmh-institute manual review findings (019e85e9)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 (suspended-login-block) passed all CI checks and is ready to merge; toggle draft=false to proceed. (source: [[2026-06-01 2120 — BMH Institute PR79 suspended-login-block A5 appr (60792029)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 (suspended-login-block) merged into bmh-institute main; post-merge CI and Vercel green, rollback tag recorded, lane closed. (source: [[2026-06-01 2121 — BMH Institute PR #79 merged, post-merge gates gr (019e860c)]])\n- 2026-06-01 — PR #79 merged (head a737fac); E2E write-path rerun pending with explicit env mapping; branch drift and stale process blockers