+---
+
+# Generate Lesson 17 wallet scene asset
+
+## Goal
+
+Generate one course scene PNG at `course-assets/scenes/module-17/m17_L17_b10_wallet.png`.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Use the attached BMH course doodle references and cast/object boards.
+- Create one 1600 x 900 PNG.
+- Match the locked sticker-sheet doodle style: thick wobbly black outlines, flat fills, rounded corners, and cornflower-blue `#62b3f3` background.
+- Use only yellow, orange, cream, white, and black, except flat money-green on the cash bills only.
+- Compose a two-panel split scene divided by one simple vertical black line.
+- Left panel: one wilted drooping cream lead-card slipping downward, sad, neglected, slightly faded.
+- Right panel: one upright cream card with one large bold black checkmark inside a yellow rounded square, with an open cream wallet below it.
+- Wallet contains three flat green cash bills with thick black outlines.
+- Leave clean bottom-center blue space for code-rendered Sticker text.
+- Avoid people, letters, words, numbers, dollar signs, labels, readable paperwork, ambient doodles, decorative clutter, shadows, gradients, lighting, texture, and perspective.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Confirm the file exists at the requested path.
+- Confirm the file is a PNG at 1600 x 900.
+- Visually inspect for the left wilted lead-card, right checked card, open wallet, and three green bills.
+- Confirm no people, readable text, numbers, dollar signs, or decorative ambient doodles.
+- Confirm the bottom-center region is clean cornflower blue for the Sticker overlay.

